Oh, Mom, they're no fun.

140
00:13:09,224 --> 00:13:12,824
Wanna see me
be a leopard? [growls]

141
00:13:12,904 --> 00:13:15,144
Why don't you just come up
with your own sound?

142
00:13:15,224 --> 00:13:17,584
- [screeches]
- Hmm.

143
00:13:17,624 --> 00:13:19,944
[silly noises]

144
00:13:22,104 --> 00:13:24,184
[all] Kala.

145
00:13:28,424 --> 00:13:29,704
Oops.

146
00:13:29,744 --> 00:13:31,584
[growls]

147
00:13:31,664 --> 00:13:33,144
[nervous laughter]

148
00:13:33,224 --> 00:13:35,904
Tarzan! Thank goodness
you're all right!

149
00:13:36,024 --> 00:13:39,864
Kala and I have
been so worried.

150
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:42,824
Thank you. Thank you so much
for finding him, Kerchak.

151
00:13:42,944 --> 00:13:45,984
You are such a wise
and caring leader.

152
00:13:46,904 --> 00:13:48,224
[whispers] Run.

153
00:13:48,784 --> 00:13:50,664
Um. Hmm.

154
00:13:52,584 --> 00:13:53,944
Hello.

155
00:13:54,024 --> 00:13:55,544
- Are you thick in the head?
- What?

156
00:13:55,624 --> 00:13:57,304
How many times
do I have to tell you?

157
00:13:57,384 --> 00:14:01,064
If you want Kerchak
to like you,
stay away from him.

158
00:14:01,104 --> 00:14:02,664
[laughing] Come on,
step on it!

159
00:14:02,744 --> 00:14:04,424
Last one there
is a dung beetle!

160
00:14:04,464 --> 00:14:06,504
Yeah, the first one's
gotta eat it.

161
00:14:06,584 --> 00:14:07,784
Terk, can I come?

162
00:14:07,864 --> 00:14:09,464
Well, you could
if you could keep up,

163
00:14:09,544 --> 00:14:12,104
but, you know,
you can't really keep up.

164
00:14:12,104 --> 00:14:15,944
Wait up, guys!
Wait up! Right behind you!

165
00:14:18,824 --> 00:14:21,304
[elephants trumpeting]

166
00:14:24,144 --> 00:14:25,864
[chimp] You're standing
on my spleen.

167
00:14:25,944 --> 00:14:27,904
Take that!
Stop hitting yourself.

168
00:14:27,984 --> 00:14:31,344
Stop hitting yourself.
Stop hitting yourself.

169
00:14:31,424 --> 00:14:34,864
♪ The fun has arrived ♪

170
00:14:34,944 --> 00:14:37,584
- Thank you very much.
- Hey, what took you so long?

171
00:14:37,664 --> 00:14:39,304
I had a little
pest control problem,

172
00:14:39,384 --> 00:14:42,304
but it's all
taken care of. Whoa!

173
00:14:42,344 --> 00:14:44,664
Hi, guys.

174
00:14:44,704 --> 00:14:47,144
Terk, what is this,
some kind of joke?

175
00:14:47,184 --> 00:14:50,184
Tell me I'm not looking
at the hairless wonder.

176
00:14:50,264 --> 00:14:53,344
Well, Terk said I could come
along if I could keep up.

177
00:14:53,424 --> 00:14:56,664
- No, no.
- Terk. Come on.

178
00:14:56,704 --> 00:15:00,824
I'll handle this, guys, okay?
Listen, buddy. Come here.

179
00:15:00,904 --> 00:15:04,144
We got a tiny, little,
itsy-bitsy problem here, okay?

180
00:15:04,184 --> 00:15:07,344
Personally, I'd love
to hang out with you.
You know I would.

181
00:15:07,384 --> 00:15:10,504
But the guys... they need
a little convincing, you know?

182
00:15:10,584 --> 00:15:14,344
- Okay, what do I gotta do?
- Do? What do you gotta do?

183
00:15:14,384 --> 00:15:17,624
- [laughing] It's so stupid.
- What?

184
00:15:17,704 --> 00:15:22,424
Well, you gotta...
you gotta go get a hair.

185
00:15:22,544 --> 00:15:24,424
- A hair?
- [Terk] Yeah, a hair.

186
00:15:24,504 --> 00:15:27,024
- Uh-huh.
- [trumpeting]

187
00:15:27,064 --> 00:15:29,584
An elephant hair.

188
00:15:29,664 --> 00:15:31,344
[angry trumpeting]

189
00:15:34,024 --> 00:15:35,704
An elephant hair?

190
00:15:35,784 --> 00:15:38,464
Like I said,
it's stupid, right?

191
00:15:38,544 --> 00:15:41,264
Listen, take it from me.
Go home. Okay?

192
00:15:41,344 --> 00:15:43,464
Who needs this aggravation?

193
00:15:43,544 --> 00:15:46,144
You know, I'm probably
gonna leave soon myself.

194
00:15:46,224 --> 00:15:49,184
You go, I'll catch up,
all right?

195
00:15:49,224 --> 00:15:52,424
You see? Leave it to me.
I told you I could...

196
00:15:52,504 --> 00:15:54,944
- Tarzan! Tarzan!
- [Tarzan shouting]

197
00:15:55,024 --> 00:15:56,704
No!

198
00:16:03,224 --> 00:16:04,624
[all] Oooh!

199
00:16:04,704 --> 00:16:06,344
That one hurt him.

200
00:16:23,384 --> 00:16:26,104
Look! Oh! Oh! There he is!

201
00:16:26,144 --> 00:16:27,744
He's alive!

202
00:16:27,864 --> 00:16:30,744
- Hey, guys!
- [all] Hi.

203
00:16:30,824 --> 00:16:33,264
- [laughter]
- [Terk] Oh, no. No, no.

204
00:16:33,344 --> 00:16:36,744
Come back! Come back.

205
00:16:36,784 --> 00:16:38,344
This guy's great.

206
00:16:38,424 --> 00:16:41,264
If he lives, you should
bring him around more often.

207
00:16:41,304 --> 00:16:43,944
Come on, come on.
Let's go get a better seat.
STYLE
::cue()

208
00:16:46,904 --> 00:16:49,624
[elephant] You can never get
enough sleep, let me tell you.

209
00:16:49,664 --> 00:16:51,224
- [elephant 2] I get enough.
- Mom?

210
00:16:51,304 --> 00:16:52,944
[elephant] It burns up
the calories.

211
00:16:53,024 --> 00:16:55,264
Are you sure
this water's sanitary?

212
00:16:55,304 --> 00:16:58,224
It looks questionable to me.

213
00:16:58,304 --> 00:17:00,424
It's fine, honey.

214
00:17:00,464 --> 00:17:04,584
Ick! But what about bacteria?

215
00:17:04,624 --> 00:17:08,304
Tantor, can't you see
Mummy's talking?

216
00:17:09,384 --> 00:17:10,424
[gasps]

217
00:17:10,464 --> 00:17:12,264
[elephants chatting]

218
00:17:12,304 --> 00:17:15,344
Huh! Watch out!
There's something swimming!

219
00:17:15,424 --> 00:17:16,904
It's coming right at you!

220
00:17:16,984 --> 00:17:19,144
Honey, Mummy's
losing her patience.

221
00:17:19,184 --> 00:17:21,544
But this time
I really see something.

222
00:17:21,664 --> 00:17:22,664
[mom] Oh, boy.

223
00:17:23,344 --> 00:17:25,464
Piranha! It's a piranha!

224
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:29,024
Sweetheart, there are no
piranhas in Africa.

225
00:17:29,104 --> 00:17:30,584
Don't tell the kid that.

226
00:17:30,664 --> 00:17:32,544
Of course there are
piranhas in Africa.

227
00:17:32,624 --> 00:17:35,464
No, she's right.
They're native
to South America.

228
00:17:35,504 --> 00:17:37,064
- Get outta here.
- It's true.

229
00:17:37,144 --> 00:17:38,664
- No way.
- Come on, now.

230
00:17:38,744 --> 00:17:40,504
Think I'd be here
if there were?

231
00:17:40,584 --> 00:17:42,624
Ah! It's right behind you!
Run!

232
00:17:42,664 --> 00:17:47,544
For the last time, honey,
there are no piranhas in...

233
00:17:47,624 --> 00:17:49,024
My butt!

234
00:17:50,024 --> 00:17:51,064
Told you!

235
00:17:51,144 --> 00:17:52,304
There's something on my butt!

236
00:17:52,344 --> 00:17:55,064
- What is it?
- Are there any more of them?

237
00:17:55,144 --> 00:17:56,864
Ah!

238
00:17:56,944 --> 00:18:00,904
- What is it?
- It's a piranha.

239
00:18:04,184 --> 00:18:05,184
[gasping]

240
00:18:05,264 --> 00:18:06,704
[all] Piranha!

241
00:18:08,944 --> 00:18:11,384
Tantor, where are you?

242
00:18:21,824 --> 00:18:23,864
- He's dead.
- [trumpeting]

243
00:18:23,944 --> 00:18:25,904
We're dead!

244
00:18:31,704 --> 00:18:34,744
We didn't do it!
They're the ones!

245
00:18:42,064 --> 00:18:44,384
[screeching]

246
00:18:52,584 --> 00:18:54,624
Oh, thank you, Kerchak.

247
00:18:58,144 --> 00:18:59,904
Tarzan, buddy!
Buddy, come on!

248
00:18:59,984 --> 00:19:02,224
Tarzan, don't die on me!
Don't die on me!

249
00:19:02,264 --> 00:19:03,424
You weren't supposed to do it!

250
00:19:03,464 --> 00:19:04,704
Get away from there.

251
00:19:04,744 --> 00:19:07,704
Don't you know a piranha
can strip your flesh
in seconds?

252
00:19:07,744 --> 00:19:11,064
What? He's not a piranha!
He's...

253
00:19:11,104 --> 00:19:13,304
- [coughing]
- [Terk] He's alive!

254
00:19:13,384 --> 00:19:15,624
He's alive! He's alive!

255
00:19:15,704 --> 00:19:17,664
- He's alive!
- He's...

256
00:19:17,784 --> 00:19:19,104
You idiot!

257
00:19:19,184 --> 00:19:22,104
You nearly gave me a
heart attack! You happy?

258
00:19:22,144 --> 00:19:23,184
Uh-huh.

259
00:19:23,264 --> 00:19:24,584
You...

260
00:19:24,704 --> 00:19:26,944
I don't believe it.
You got the hair?

261
00:19:27,024 --> 00:19:31,784
Is that what
this is all about?
I got a whole tail of them.

262
00:19:31,824 --> 00:19:33,744
- [Kala] Tarzan?
- [ape mother] Terkina?

263
00:19:33,784 --> 00:19:35,264
[Terk] Oh, no.

264
00:19:35,384 --> 00:19:37,944
- Who's that?
- [both] My mom.

265
00:19:37,984 --> 00:19:39,624
- [Kala] Tarzan.
- Hi.

266
00:19:39,664 --> 00:19:42,064
- Hi, Aunt Kala.
- Oh, you scared me!

267
00:19:42,104 --> 00:19:44,344
- What happened?
- Well, I...

268
00:19:44,424 --> 00:19:46,464
Um, it's sort of a long...
It's involved.

269
00:19:46,504 --> 00:19:48,704
Because what happened,
it was a weird...

270
00:19:48,784 --> 00:19:50,744
What happened?

271
00:19:53,104 --> 00:19:56,344
- It was my fault, Kerchak.
- Tarzan.

272
00:19:56,424 --> 00:20:01,184
We were playing, and...
Well, I'm sorry, Kerchak.

273
00:20:01,264 --> 00:20:03,304
You almost killed someone.

274
00:20:03,384 --> 00:20:05,544
- It was an accident.
- He's only a child.

275
00:20:05,624 --> 00:20:08,104
That's no excuse.
You can't keep defending him.

276
00:20:08,144 --> 00:20:09,224
But he'll learn.

277
00:20:09,304 --> 00:20:11,144
He will not. You can't
learn to be one of us.

278
00:20:11,224 --> 00:20:14,024
- You never give him a chance.
- Give him a chance?

279
00:20:14,104 --> 00:20:18,144
[Kerchak] Kala, look at him.
He will never be one of us.

280
00:20:18,224 --> 00:20:20,104
[Kala] Kerchak!

281
00:20:20,664 --> 00:20:22,504
Tarzan.

282
00:20:23,104 --> 00:20:24,984
[sighs]

283
00:20:48,424 --> 00:20:51,944
[panting, shouting]

284
00:21:04,544 --> 00:21:07,144
[grunting]
STYLE
::cue()

285
00:21:13,064 --> 00:21:15,664
Tarzan,
what are you doing?

286
00:21:16,224 --> 00:21:18,064
Why am I so different?

287
00:21:18,144 --> 00:21:20,304
Because you're covered
with mud, that's why.

288
00:21:20,384 --> 00:21:22,224
No! Kerchak said
I didn't belong in...

289
00:21:22,304 --> 00:21:23,504
[Kala] Close your mouth.

290
00:21:23,544 --> 00:21:25,864
Kerchak said I don't
belong in the family.

291
00:21:25,904 --> 00:21:28,384
Never mind what Kerchak said.

292
00:21:28,424 --> 00:21:31,344
- Hold still.
- But look at me!

293
00:21:33,584 --> 00:21:35,744
I am, Tarzan.

294
00:21:35,824 --> 00:21:37,544
And do you know what I see?

295
00:21:37,584 --> 00:21:41,024
I see two eyes, like mine,

296
00:21:41,064 --> 00:21:45,544
and a nose, somewhere. Ah!

297
00:21:45,584 --> 00:21:47,064
Here.

298
00:21:47,144 --> 00:21:49,864
Two ears.

299
00:21:49,904 --> 00:21:53,384
- And let's see, what else?
- Two hands?

300
00:21:53,424 --> 00:21:55,104
That's right. [laughs]

301
00:22:06,264 --> 00:22:08,144
[sighs]

302
00:22:11,424 --> 00:22:14,024
Close your eyes.

303
00:22:14,104 --> 00:22:16,504
Now, forget what you see.

304
00:22:16,584 --> 00:22:18,504
What do you feel?

305
00:22:19,784 --> 00:22:21,264
My heart.

306
00:22:21,304 --> 00:22:23,224
Come here.

307
00:22:24,784 --> 00:22:26,784
- Your heart.
- See?

308
00:22:26,824 --> 00:22:29,384
We're exactly the same.

309
00:22:31,944 --> 00:22:34,904
Kerchak just can't see that.

310
00:22:37,064 --> 00:22:38,984
I'll make him see it.

311
00:22:39,024 --> 00:22:41,864
I'll be the best ape ever.

312
00:22:41,944 --> 00:22:44,184
[chuckles] Oh, I bet you will.

313
00:22:57,744 --> 00:23:01,304
♪ Oh, the power to be strong ♪

314
00:23:01,384 --> 00:23:04,904
♪ And the wisdom to be wise ♪

315
00:23:04,984 --> 00:23:09,824
♪ All these things
will come to you in time ♪

316
00:23:11,304 --> 00:23:14,504
♪ On this journey
that you're making ♪

317
00:23:14,584 --> 00:23:18,304
♪ There'll be answers
that you'll seek ♪

318
00:23:18,344 --> 00:23:21,504
♪ And it's you
who'll climb the mountain ♪

319
00:23:21,544 --> 00:23:25,144
♪ It's you
who'll reach the peak ♪

320
00:23:25,184 --> 00:23:28,624
♪ Son of Man,
look to the sky ♪

321
00:23:28,664 --> 00:23:31,864
♪ Lift your spirit
Set it free ♪

322
00:23:31,944 --> 00:23:35,304
♪ Someday you'll
walk tall with pride ♪

323
00:23:35,344 --> 00:23:40,264
♪ Son of Man
A man in time you'll be ♪

324
00:23:51,864 --> 00:23:55,064
♪ Though there's no one there
to guide you ♪

325
00:23:55,144 --> 00:23:58,704
♪ No one to take your hand ♪

326
00:23:58,784 --> 00:24:02,104
♪ But with faith
and understanding ♪

327
00:24:02,184 --> 00:24:05,984
♪ You will journey
from boy to man ♪

328
00:24:06,064 --> 00:24:09,424
♪ Son of Man,
look to the sky ♪

329
00:24:09,504 --> 00:24:12,664
♪ Lift your spirit
Set it free ♪

330
00:24:12,744 --> 00:24:15,984
♪ Someday you'll
walk tall with pride ♪

331
00:24:16,064 --> 00:24:20,944
♪ Son of Man
A man in time you'll be ♪

332
00:24:26,184 --> 00:24:29,304
♪ In learning you will teach ♪

333
00:24:29,384 --> 00:24:32,904
♪ And in teaching
you will learn ♪

334
00:24:32,944 --> 00:24:37,744
♪ You'll find your place
beside the ones you love ♪

335
00:24:39,544 --> 00:24:42,824
♪ Oh, and all the things
you dreamed of ♪

336
00:24:42,904 --> 00:24:46,504
♪ The visions that you saw ♪

337
00:24:46,584 --> 00:24:49,664
♪ Well, the time
is drawing near now ♪

338
00:24:49,784 --> 00:24:53,344
♪ It's yours to claim it all ♪

339
00:24:53,424 --> 00:24:56,784
♪ Son of Man
Look to the sky ♪

340
00:24:56,824 --> 00:25:00,104
♪ Lift your spirit
Set it free ♪

341
00:25:00,144 --> 00:25:03,904
♪ Someday you'll
walk tall with pride ♪

342
00:25:03,944 --> 00:25:08,984
♪ Son of Man
A man in time you'll be ♪

343
00:25:15,864 --> 00:25:17,384
♪ Son of Man ♪

344
00:25:17,464 --> 00:25:22,344
♪ Son of Man's
a man for all to see ♪♪
STYLE
::cue()

345
00:25:39,984 --> 00:25:42,184
Don't even think about it.

346
00:25:42,264 --> 00:25:43,784
[blows raspberry]

347
00:25:43,864 --> 00:25:45,024
How'd you know it was me?

348
00:25:45,104 --> 00:25:47,104
I'm your mother.
I know everything.

349
00:25:47,144 --> 00:25:50,104
- Where have you been?
- I thought you knew
everything.

350
00:25:51,184 --> 00:25:52,824
- [growling]
- Hey, Auntie K.

351
00:25:52,864 --> 00:25:54,824
You're looking
remarkably groomed today.

352
00:25:54,864 --> 00:25:56,664
- Hello, Terk.
- [roars]

353
00:25:56,704 --> 00:25:59,264
[Terk] Not the neck!
Not the neck there, T.

354
00:26:01,024 --> 00:26:03,704
[Terk] Watch it! Oh! Ow!

355
00:26:05,584 --> 00:26:09,184
Okay, it's all fun and games
till someone loses an eye.

356
00:26:09,264 --> 00:26:11,864
[Tantor] Please stop.
Somebody's gonna
get hurt here.

357
00:26:11,944 --> 00:26:14,504
- [Tantor] And it's always me.
- [Terk] Cramp in the calf.

358
00:26:14,584 --> 00:26:17,024
- Please!
- Okay. Okay, you win.

359
00:26:17,104 --> 00:26:21,544
Ow! Okay, okay, you win.
Hello! Down here.
Yo, yo! Let go!

360
00:26:21,624 --> 00:26:24,584
- Oh, sorry, Terk.
- What kind of animal are you?

361
00:26:24,664 --> 00:26:27,344
You know, I been thinking
lately that maybe Tarzan

362
00:26:27,384 --> 00:26:29,504
could be some
subspecies of elephant.

363
00:26:29,544 --> 00:26:31,544
[Terk] What are you, crazy?
An elephant?

364
00:26:31,624 --> 00:26:35,504
[Tantor] Listen to me.
Think about it. He enjoys
a peanut, I enjoy a peanut.

365
00:26:35,544 --> 00:26:37,384
He looks nothing like you.

366
00:26:37,464 --> 00:26:39,224
[roaring]

367
00:26:58,224 --> 00:27:00,104
[low growling]

368
00:27:05,264 --> 00:27:06,864
- [ferocious roar]
- Ahhhh!

369
00:27:13,504 --> 00:27:15,624
[apes screeching, hooting]

370
00:28:14,624 --> 00:28:16,144
[Tarzan yelps]

371
00:28:31,144 --> 00:28:33,624
[rustling]

372
00:28:34,544 --> 00:28:36,584
[grunting]

373
00:28:51,824 --> 00:28:54,064
[triumphant grunting]

374
00:29:03,704 --> 00:29:06,504
[Tarzan yells]

375
00:29:25,024 --> 00:29:27,824
[Terk] Okay everybody,
move aside. Outta my way.

376
00:29:27,864 --> 00:29:31,064
Best friend coming through.
That would be me.

377
00:29:31,064 --> 00:29:33,264
And you, don't make
a habit of that, okay?

378
00:29:33,344 --> 00:29:35,864
There are other ways
of getting attention.

379
00:29:35,944 --> 00:29:37,864
- I'll try to remember that.
- All right.

380
00:29:37,984 --> 00:29:41,144
I was right behind you
if you needed me.
I had you covered.

381
00:30:12,824 --> 00:30:15,064
[gunshot]
STYLE
::cue()

382
00:30:15,104 --> 00:30:17,224
[birds crying]

383
00:30:18,744 --> 00:30:20,264
What was that?

384
00:30:20,304 --> 00:30:23,064
I... It wasn't me, I swear.

385
00:30:23,104 --> 00:30:25,904
- [Tantor] Okay, maybe it was.
- [Kerchak] Everyone,

386
00:30:25,944 --> 00:30:27,704
let's move.

387
00:30:29,264 --> 00:30:31,464
[apes grunting]

388
00:30:31,544 --> 00:30:33,744
[gunshot]

389
00:30:45,904 --> 00:30:48,464
[sniffing]

390
00:31:10,664 --> 00:31:14,224
- [coughing, choking]
- [gunshot]

391
00:31:15,824 --> 00:31:19,344
[Clayton] I was reminded of a
safari I led up the Zambezi.

392
00:31:19,464 --> 00:31:23,544
Marvelous.
Lots of hunting, yes.
Bang, bang, bang, bang, bang.

393
00:31:23,624 --> 00:31:25,544
Wildebeest everywhere.

394
00:31:25,624 --> 00:31:30,824
Two bearers loading
three rifles for me,
blasting away.

395
00:31:30,904 --> 00:31:34,504
That's when I knew
I was born for Africa

396
00:31:34,584 --> 00:31:37,624
and Africa was created for...

397
00:31:39,624 --> 00:31:41,344
[gunshot]

398
00:31:45,864 --> 00:31:47,344
[Porter] Clayton?

399
00:31:47,384 --> 00:31:49,704
[panting] Clayton...
Oh, there you are.

400
00:31:49,704 --> 00:31:52,744
What is it?
What is it, Clayton?
Are we in danger?

401
00:31:52,824 --> 00:31:54,504
I thought I saw something.

402
00:31:54,584 --> 00:31:58,144
Is it a Hippopotamus
amphibious or
a Rhinoceros bihornus?

403
00:31:58,184 --> 00:31:59,784
[Clayton] Professor,
don't move!

404
00:31:59,864 --> 00:32:01,984
- Oh, right.
- [Jane] Daddy?

405
00:32:02,024 --> 00:32:04,264
Ow, ow, ow!

406
00:32:04,344 --> 00:32:07,744
Daddy, what's all
the hullabaloo about? [grunts]

407
00:32:08,664 --> 00:32:10,944
[Jane] Ow! Ah!

408
00:32:11,024 --> 00:32:12,384
What is it, Daddy?

409
00:32:12,464 --> 00:32:15,504
Mr. Clayton asked me not
to move. He saw something.

410
00:32:16,824 --> 00:32:18,584
Uh... Ooh!

411
00:32:18,664 --> 00:32:19,944
I moved.

412
00:32:20,024 --> 00:32:22,904
Uh, Mr. Clayton?
Sorry, excuse me.

413
00:32:22,984 --> 00:32:26,504
But my father and I came
on this expedition
to study gorillas,

414
00:32:26,544 --> 00:32:29,584
and I believe your shooting
might be scaring them off.

415
00:32:29,664 --> 00:32:32,064
You hired me to protect you,
Miss Porter,

416
00:32:32,144 --> 00:32:34,184
and protect you I shall.

417
00:32:34,224 --> 00:32:36,424
And you're doing
a marvelous job of it.

418
00:32:36,504 --> 00:32:37,744
But we only
have a short time

419
00:32:37,824 --> 00:32:40,224
before the ship returns,
you see...

420
00:32:40,304 --> 00:32:43,824
Jane! Jane, do you realize
what you're standing in?

421
00:32:43,904 --> 00:32:46,344
- A gorilla's nest!
- [gasps] Daddy!

422
00:32:46,424 --> 00:32:49,824
At last!
Our first sign in days.

423
00:32:49,904 --> 00:32:52,544
Do you think the beasts
could be nearby?

424
00:32:52,584 --> 00:32:54,744
Could be. Why, I mean,
there's the evidence.

425
00:32:54,784 --> 00:32:57,264
[Porter stammering] They
can't be very far, anyway.

426
00:32:57,344 --> 00:32:59,064
Look! Over there and there...

427
00:32:59,184 --> 00:33:00,784
[Porter] Where?
Yes, more nests!

428
00:33:00,864 --> 00:33:02,744
- I see them!
- Just as you predicted!

429
00:33:02,824 --> 00:33:04,384
Family groups!

430
00:33:04,424 --> 00:33:06,424
Oh, Jane, I love you.

431
00:33:06,464 --> 00:33:09,504
- [laughter]
- Family groups?

432
00:33:09,584 --> 00:33:12,344
[laughing] Excuse me,
but these are wild beasts

433
00:33:12,424 --> 00:33:15,264
that would sooner tear your
head off than look at you.

434
00:33:15,344 --> 00:33:16,424
On the contrary, Mr. Clayton.

435
00:33:16,504 --> 00:33:19,864
Daddy's theory is that
these are social creatures,
not monsters.

436
00:33:19,944 --> 00:33:22,104
[bird squawking]

437
00:33:24,624 --> 00:33:27,864
Mr. Clayton, please.
What if it's a gorilla?

438
00:33:27,944 --> 00:33:29,944
It's no gorilla.

439
00:33:32,464 --> 00:33:35,344
Mmm.
Perhaps we should press on.

440
00:33:35,424 --> 00:33:36,464
Yes, indeed.

441
00:33:36,504 --> 00:33:38,504
Now, we should keep
heading west,

442
00:33:38,584 --> 00:33:40,304
following
the Ganoderma ablonatum.

443
00:33:40,384 --> 00:33:42,144
[Clayton]
Excellent, professor.

444
00:33:42,224 --> 00:33:45,184
I could've used your expertise
on my last safari.

445
00:33:45,264 --> 00:33:47,144
I was in the mountainous
region of Zambia.

446
00:33:47,184 --> 00:33:50,464
- [cries out] Oh!
- [Clayton]
Yes, very dangerous.

447
00:33:50,504 --> 00:33:52,384
Oh!

448
00:33:52,464 --> 00:33:55,544
Are you what all
the fuss was about?

449
00:33:55,624 --> 00:33:58,544
[whispering] Daddy!
Daddy, quick!

450
00:33:58,664 --> 00:34:00,744
No, wait. Hold still.

451
00:34:00,824 --> 00:34:02,304
Oh, my good...

452
00:34:02,384 --> 00:34:07,144
You may not be a gorilla,
but you are
one sweet little...

453
00:34:11,904 --> 00:34:13,584
There you go.
What do you think?

454
00:34:15,104 --> 00:34:17,144
[squeals]

455
00:34:17,264 --> 00:34:19,704
What? Oh!

456
00:34:19,784 --> 00:34:21,424
[Jane] Why, you little...

457
00:34:21,504 --> 00:34:25,584
Well, this is
absolutely peachy.
Come to study gorillas

458
00:34:25,664 --> 00:34:29,184
and get my sketchbook
pinched by a baboon.

459
00:34:29,224 --> 00:34:31,744
[grunting, laughing]

460
00:34:36,504 --> 00:34:38,184
Give me that!

461
00:34:40,024 --> 00:34:41,624
Come on now, enough of this.

462
00:34:41,704 --> 00:34:43,664
I want this paper
on the count of three.

463
00:34:43,704 --> 00:34:45,304
One.

464
00:34:45,344 --> 00:34:47,184
Two.

465
00:34:47,224 --> 00:34:49,464
Oh, look, bananas!

466
00:34:49,544 --> 00:34:53,424
[laughing] I can't believe
you fell for that one.

467
00:34:53,504 --> 00:34:54,944
[crying]

468
00:34:55,024 --> 00:34:58,024
No, no, don't give me
those crocodile tears.

469
00:34:58,104 --> 00:34:59,864
What would your parents
have to say?

470
00:34:59,904 --> 00:35:01,144
- [roaring]
- [yelps]
STYLE
::cue()

471
00:35:04,424 --> 00:35:06,424
You see, I told you
they'd be cross.

472
00:35:06,504 --> 00:35:09,384
Go easy on him.
Children will be children.

473
00:35:29,224 --> 00:35:30,584
[Jane] I'm flying!

474
00:35:30,624 --> 00:35:34,144
What on earth am I...
[gasps, screams]

475
00:35:35,184 --> 00:35:37,864
[Jane] Get off! Get off!

476
00:35:42,744 --> 00:35:45,624
Put me down! Put me down!

477
00:35:45,704 --> 00:35:48,104
[Jane] No, pick me up,
pick me up!

478
00:35:52,584 --> 00:35:54,824
[Jane] Help!

479
00:35:54,904 --> 00:35:56,744
Oh, no!

480
00:35:56,824 --> 00:35:59,304
[Jane screaming]

481
00:36:09,864 --> 00:36:12,344
[laughing]

482
00:36:14,784 --> 00:36:17,104
Unhand me, monkey!

483
00:36:37,904 --> 00:36:39,144
Over there!

484
00:37:10,624 --> 00:37:13,144
[chattering]

485
00:37:14,344 --> 00:37:16,304
[chattering]

486
00:37:27,184 --> 00:37:28,864
[panting]

487
00:37:28,904 --> 00:37:32,344
I'm in a tree with a man
who talks to monkeys.

488
00:37:33,784 --> 00:37:35,384
I can't do this. I can't...

489
00:37:35,504 --> 00:37:38,144
Oh! This is good.
This is very good.

490
00:37:38,184 --> 00:37:40,344
I... Oh! Wait.

491
00:37:40,384 --> 00:37:43,624
One, two. [yelps]

492
00:37:45,464 --> 00:37:47,584
It can't get any worse,
can it?

493
00:37:47,664 --> 00:37:49,264
[thunder crashes]

494
00:37:51,064 --> 00:37:53,264
Obviously it can.

495
00:37:56,304 --> 00:37:57,384
[shrieks]

496
00:38:01,904 --> 00:38:04,744
Stay back. No, don't...
Don't come any closer.

497
00:38:04,824 --> 00:38:06,064
Please, don't.

498
00:38:06,104 --> 00:38:07,784
What are you...
What are you doing?

499
00:38:07,864 --> 00:38:12,104
[laughing] No, please don't.
That tickles.

500
00:38:12,184 --> 00:38:14,064
No, get off, get off.
Get off!

501
00:38:15,104 --> 00:38:16,664
[Jane] It serves you right.

502
00:38:16,744 --> 00:38:19,224
Stay away from me,
like a very good wild man.

503
00:38:19,304 --> 00:38:21,744
You stay. I'm warning you.

504
00:38:21,824 --> 00:38:23,704
My father won't
take kindly to you...

505
00:38:23,744 --> 00:38:27,024
No. That's...
Now, that's close enough.

506
00:38:27,064 --> 00:38:30,384
How dare you? What...?
STYLE
::cue()

507
00:39:05,504 --> 00:39:09,224
[gasps] Oh! Um...

508
00:39:09,304 --> 00:39:12,304
- [heartbeat]
- Oh...

509
00:39:15,944 --> 00:39:17,184
Oh, dear.

510
00:39:17,264 --> 00:39:19,584
Oh, dear, oh, dear.
Oh, dear.

511
00:39:20,424 --> 00:39:21,504
Yes, thank you.

512
00:39:21,584 --> 00:39:25,504
That's a lovely heartbeat.
It's very nice.

513
00:39:27,624 --> 00:39:29,704
- It's very nice.
- Oh, thank you.

514
00:39:29,784 --> 00:39:33,264
I can't do a thing with it
in this humidity though.
It's...

515
00:39:33,304 --> 00:39:34,744
You do speak!

516
00:39:34,824 --> 00:39:36,264
All this time
I thought you were

517
00:39:36,304 --> 00:39:38,744
a big, wild, quiet,
silent person thing.

518
00:39:38,824 --> 00:39:40,144
Why didn't you tell me?

519
00:39:40,184 --> 00:39:42,984
I must say I'm rather curious
as to who you are. I'd love...

520
00:39:44,424 --> 00:39:46,904
[grunts] Tarzan.

521
00:39:50,984 --> 00:39:53,144
Tarzan.

522
00:39:54,104 --> 00:39:55,824
Tarzan?

523
00:39:55,904 --> 00:39:57,904
[grunting]

524
00:39:59,144 --> 00:40:00,904
Oh, I see.

525
00:40:01,024 --> 00:40:03,064
Oh, I see.

526
00:40:03,144 --> 00:40:04,824
Tarzan.

527
00:40:04,944 --> 00:40:06,944
Oh, I see.

528
00:40:07,024 --> 00:40:10,504
No, no, no. No.
[clears throat]

529
00:40:10,544 --> 00:40:12,664
I'm Jane.

530
00:40:12,744 --> 00:40:17,264
No, no, no. No.
I'm Jane.

531
00:40:17,344 --> 00:40:19,064
No, no.

532
00:40:19,144 --> 00:40:22,304
Jane. Tarzan.

533
00:40:22,344 --> 00:40:24,024
Jane.

534
00:40:24,704 --> 00:40:26,104
Jane.

535
00:40:27,144 --> 00:40:29,344
- Exactly.
- [gunshot]

536
00:40:29,384 --> 00:40:30,664
Clayton!

537
00:40:33,344 --> 00:40:35,424
- [gunshot]
- Clayton.

538
00:40:35,504 --> 00:40:38,104
Extraordinary.

539
00:40:38,184 --> 00:40:42,424
Please, can you
take me to my camp?

540
00:40:42,504 --> 00:40:46,264
- [gunshot]
- Yes, Clayton. Wonderful.

541
00:40:46,344 --> 00:40:50,904
[stammering]
Um, can't we walk?

542
00:40:50,984 --> 00:40:53,744
[Tarzan] Can't we walk?!

543
00:40:55,184 --> 00:40:58,344
[all] Tarzan! Tarzan!
Where are you?

544
00:40:58,384 --> 00:41:00,424
[ape] Let's hope we find him
before Kerchak.

545
00:41:00,504 --> 00:41:01,984
[ape 2] Maybe he's lost.

546
00:41:02,064 --> 00:41:04,064
[ape 1] Or found something
more interesting.

547
00:41:04,144 --> 00:41:07,384
[Terk] Are you nuts?
What could be more
interesting than us?

548
00:41:07,424 --> 00:41:10,584
Hey, what's everybody
looking at? [gasps]

549
00:41:10,624 --> 00:41:13,224
[Tantor gasping]

550
00:41:16,744 --> 00:41:17,984
The horror!

551
00:41:18,104 --> 00:41:19,904
[whimpering] It's gruesome.
Hide me!

552
00:41:19,944 --> 00:41:23,064
Pull yourself together.
You're embarrassing me.

553
00:41:23,104 --> 00:41:25,624
These things aren't alive.

554
00:41:25,704 --> 00:41:27,744
- [laughter]
- I knew that.

555
00:41:27,864 --> 00:41:30,984
[all] Tarzan!

556
00:41:31,064 --> 00:41:32,824
Hello?

557
00:41:34,344 --> 00:41:38,784
What kind of primitive beasts
are responsible for this mess?

558
00:41:40,024 --> 00:41:42,024
Oh!

559
00:41:46,624 --> 00:41:49,104
Wow! Come here, you guys!
Come here, come here!

560
00:41:49,144 --> 00:41:51,064
- Look at this.
- What is that thing?

561
00:41:51,104 --> 00:41:53,024
- Funny. Wow.
- [dings]

562
00:41:53,104 --> 00:41:55,224
[all] Oooh!

563
00:41:57,824 --> 00:42:00,664
- [shattering]
- [Terk] Hey!

564
00:42:00,744 --> 00:42:03,064
Do it again, do it again.

565
00:42:03,144 --> 00:42:04,624
Like this?

566
00:42:04,664 --> 00:42:07,144
- [tearing]
- [Terk] Yeah!

567
00:42:09,064 --> 00:42:10,824
Yeah. Rip it!

568
00:42:12,104 --> 00:42:14,384
Ding! I love that part.

569
00:42:15,704 --> 00:42:17,904
Let me hear it, big fella.

570
00:42:17,984 --> 00:42:20,664
- [Terk] Now, hit it!
- [laughter]

571
00:42:22,144 --> 00:42:24,144
Yeah!

572
00:42:26,664 --> 00:42:28,144
Nice.

573
00:42:29,144 --> 00:42:31,224
What the heck? Bye-bye.

574
00:42:31,304 --> 00:42:33,744
Terk. [trumpets]

575
00:42:33,824 --> 00:42:35,504
Yeah, Tant.

576
00:42:35,584 --> 00:42:37,824
Now, hit it.

577
00:42:37,864 --> 00:42:40,624
- Come on, Tantor.
- [trumpets]

578
00:42:40,664 --> 00:42:42,664
[Terk] I love it.

579
00:42:42,704 --> 00:42:44,144
Stay with me, fellas.

580
00:42:44,184 --> 00:42:47,464
I feel something
happening here.

581
00:42:47,504 --> 00:42:51,864
[animals play music
with items in camp]

582
00:42:51,904 --> 00:42:56,664
[Terk] ♪ Shoo-bee-do-da-be-da
Do-be-do-da-ba-da-ba-do ♪

583
00:42:56,744 --> 00:43:02,344
[gorillas]
♪ Shoo-bee-do-da-be-da
Do-be-do-da-ba-da-ba-do ♪
STYLE
::cue()

584
00:43:02,424 --> 00:43:06,624
[all] ♪ Shoo-bee-do-da-be-da
Do-be-do-da-ba-da-ba-do ♪

585
00:43:06,704 --> 00:43:11,504
♪ Shoo-bop-she-doo ♪

586
00:43:11,544 --> 00:43:13,904
[musical clinking]

587
00:43:20,384 --> 00:43:21,944
[Terk] Yeah!

588
00:43:26,864 --> 00:43:29,224
♪ Bomp-bomp-bomp-bomp ♪

589
00:43:29,264 --> 00:43:30,904
[drums playing]

590
00:43:32,904 --> 00:43:34,704
[Terk] Yeah!

591
00:43:36,744 --> 00:43:41,264
[all] ♪ Shoo-bee-do-da-be-da
Do-be-do-da-ba-da-ba-do ♪

592
00:43:41,344 --> 00:43:44,584
♪ Shoo-bee-do-da-be-da
Do-be-do-da-ba-da-ba-do ♪

593
00:43:44,704 --> 00:43:46,664
♪ Wa-ba-ba-de-woo ♪

594
00:43:46,744 --> 00:43:49,064
[faint music]

595
00:43:49,144 --> 00:43:51,304
- [shattering]
- [Porter] Wha...?

596
00:43:51,384 --> 00:43:54,784
♪ Shoo-bop-she-doo ♪

597
00:43:55,984 --> 00:43:59,584
♪ Shoo-bop-she-doo ♪

598
00:43:59,624 --> 00:44:01,064
♪ Woo-woo! ♪

599
00:44:01,104 --> 00:44:04,184
[speeding up]
♪ Shoo-bop-she-doo ♪

600
00:44:05,544 --> 00:44:08,904
♪ Shoo-bop-she-doo ♪

601
00:44:08,984 --> 00:44:10,304
♪ Woo! ♪♪

602
00:44:10,384 --> 00:44:12,344
[trumpet trails off]

603
00:44:13,584 --> 00:44:16,384
[gasping] Gorillas!

604
00:44:18,664 --> 00:44:20,744
[grunting]

605
00:44:24,144 --> 00:44:26,064
He's one of them.

606
00:44:46,704 --> 00:44:47,824
[growl]

607
00:44:47,904 --> 00:44:50,984
- Oh, my...
- [roar]

608
00:44:54,144 --> 00:44:56,464
[Jane whimpering]

609
00:45:24,744 --> 00:45:28,224
[Porter and Clayton]
Jane!

610
00:45:30,624 --> 00:45:33,144
[Porter] Jane, where are you?

611
00:45:33,184 --> 00:45:35,504
Jane. Oh, Jane.

612
00:45:35,584 --> 00:45:37,984
- Thank goodness.
- Good heavens, what happened?

613
00:45:38,024 --> 00:45:40,344
Are you all right?
We've been everywhere.

614
00:45:40,424 --> 00:45:41,624
Oh, my goodness.

615
00:45:41,664 --> 00:45:45,504
- Daddy, I was out walking...
- Yes, yes.

616
00:45:45,544 --> 00:45:47,344
Little baby.
Little baby monkey.

617
00:45:47,384 --> 00:45:48,784
- I drew a picture.
- Go on.

618
00:45:48,864 --> 00:45:50,984
- The monkey starts crying.
- Poor baby.

619
00:45:51,024 --> 00:45:53,864
But I turned round, and
there's a whole fleet of them!

620
00:45:53,944 --> 00:45:55,584
- Of what?
- An army of monkeys!

621
00:45:55,664 --> 00:45:57,624
- A huge tree full of them...
- Monkeys?

622
00:45:57,704 --> 00:45:59,264
...screaming at me!

623
00:45:59,384 --> 00:46:02,144
Theropithecus baboonus.
She's very good at this.

624
00:46:02,184 --> 00:46:03,784
- Oh, really?
- Terrified, I was.

625
00:46:03,864 --> 00:46:07,264
Suddenly, I was swinging
in the vines, up in the air!

626
00:46:07,344 --> 00:46:08,984
- With the monkeys?
- Flying.

627
00:46:09,024 --> 00:46:11,224
- In the air.
- And I'm all surrounded.

628
00:46:11,264 --> 00:46:13,824
- What did you do?
- And, Daddy,
they took my boot!

629
00:46:13,864 --> 00:46:15,864
They took... Those are
the ones I bought you.

630
00:46:15,944 --> 00:46:17,104
And I was saved!

631
00:46:17,184 --> 00:46:21,064
I was saved by a flying
wild man in a loincloth.

632
00:46:21,104 --> 00:46:23,904
- Loincloth, good Lord.
- What is she talking about?

633
00:46:23,944 --> 00:46:27,264
I haven't the foggiest idea.
Takes after her mother,
you know.

634
00:46:27,344 --> 00:46:30,424
She'd come up with stories.
Not about men in loincloths...

635
00:46:30,504 --> 00:46:32,624
- And there were gorillas!
- Gorillas?

636
00:46:32,704 --> 00:46:33,704
They were doing...

637
00:46:33,744 --> 00:46:36,664
You saw the gorillas? Where?

638
00:46:36,744 --> 00:46:39,824
- He left with them.
- Who, dear, who?

639
00:46:40,504 --> 00:46:42,064
Tarzan.

640
00:46:42,144 --> 00:46:43,424
Tarzan?

641
00:46:43,464 --> 00:46:45,624
The ape man.
STYLE
::cue()

642
00:46:47,664 --> 00:46:49,264
[screeching]

643
00:46:49,304 --> 00:46:51,944
[Kerchak] Everyone.
We will avoid the strangers.

644
00:46:52,024 --> 00:46:54,544
Do not let them see you,
and do not seek them out.

645
00:46:54,584 --> 00:46:56,024
[Tarzan] They mean us no harm.

646
00:46:56,104 --> 00:46:57,704
Tarzan, I don't know them.

647
00:46:57,744 --> 00:46:59,264
I do. I've spent time
with them.

648
00:46:59,344 --> 00:47:01,944
You may be willing to risk
our safety, I'm not.

649
00:47:02,024 --> 00:47:04,744
Why are you threatened
by anyone different from you?

650
00:47:07,304 --> 00:47:12,024
Protect this family,
and stay away from them.

651
00:47:15,264 --> 00:47:17,784
Tarzan, for once,
listen to Kerchak.

652
00:47:17,864 --> 00:47:21,024
Why didn't you tell me
there were creatures
that look like me?

653
00:47:29,824 --> 00:47:32,584
[Jane] Well, he didn't
stand upright. He sort of...

654
00:47:32,744 --> 00:47:34,264
- ...crouched.
- Really?

655
00:47:34,304 --> 00:47:36,224
He supported his weight
on his knuckles.

656
00:47:36,304 --> 00:47:39,264
- On the knuckles.
- See? Exactly like a gorilla.

657
00:47:39,304 --> 00:47:42,184
- Extraordinary.
- It was amazing!

658
00:47:42,264 --> 00:47:44,224
He'd bend his
elbows out like this.

659
00:47:44,304 --> 00:47:45,624
And then he walks, like this.

660
00:47:45,704 --> 00:47:48,824
Oh, I see! Like Aunt Isabel.

661
00:47:48,904 --> 00:47:50,824
- [laughter]
- [Porter] Ba, ba, ba, ba, ba.

662
00:47:50,864 --> 00:47:52,344
- [Porter] This is capital!
- Hmm.

663
00:47:52,424 --> 00:47:54,824
Janey-Jane, what a discovery!

664
00:47:54,904 --> 00:47:57,144
A man with no language,
no human behavior...

665
00:47:57,224 --> 00:47:59,664
And no respect
for personal boundaries.

666
00:47:59,744 --> 00:48:02,064
- How do you mean?
- He was this close, Daddy.

667
00:48:02,144 --> 00:48:03,384
Staring at me.

668
00:48:03,464 --> 00:48:06,744
He seemed confused at first,

669
00:48:06,824 --> 00:48:09,384
as if he's never seen
another human before.

670
00:48:09,464 --> 00:48:14,664
And his eyes were intense
and focused, and...

671
00:48:15,704 --> 00:48:18,864
[Jane] I've never seen
such eyes.

672
00:48:21,064 --> 00:48:25,424
Oh, shall I leave you and the
blackboard alone for a moment?

673
00:48:25,504 --> 00:48:28,384
Daddy, stop it.
The point is,

674
00:48:28,464 --> 00:48:31,584
think of what we could learn
from him. We must find him.

675
00:48:31,704 --> 00:48:33,064
Oh!

676
00:48:33,144 --> 00:48:36,864
Professor, you are here
to find gorillas,

677
00:48:36,944 --> 00:48:39,544
not indulge
some girlish fantasy.

678
00:48:39,584 --> 00:48:42,304
Fantasy? I didn't imagine him.

679
00:48:42,344 --> 00:48:43,624
Tarzan is...

680
00:48:43,704 --> 00:48:46,344
- [gasps]
- ...real.

681
00:48:46,424 --> 00:48:48,944
Ah! [stammering] It's him!

682
00:48:49,024 --> 00:48:50,744
It's him, it's him. Tarzan!

683
00:48:50,824 --> 00:48:52,544
- Professor, Jane, stand back!
- Wait!

684
00:48:52,584 --> 00:48:54,704
- No!
- [gunshot]

685
00:48:54,744 --> 00:48:56,384
[Tarzan] Clayton.

686
00:48:58,544 --> 00:49:00,664
- Clayton.
- Ah! [laughing]

687
00:49:00,704 --> 00:49:03,064
Have we met?

688
00:49:04,104 --> 00:49:05,864
How does he know my name?

689
00:49:05,944 --> 00:49:08,464
He thinks it means
the sound of a gunshot.

690
00:49:08,544 --> 00:49:12,664
- Jane.
- Yes. Hello, Tarzan.

691
00:49:12,744 --> 00:49:14,984
I see what you mean
about personal boundaries.

692
00:49:15,064 --> 00:49:17,704
What's he doing?

693
00:49:18,704 --> 00:49:20,584
[Porter] Look at him, Jane.

694
00:49:20,624 --> 00:49:22,704
Moves like an ape,
but looks like a man.

695
00:49:22,744 --> 00:49:25,744
He could be the missing link.

696
00:49:25,784 --> 00:49:29,024
Or our link to the gorillas.

697
00:49:29,064 --> 00:49:30,864
Ah! Yes, yes.

698
00:49:30,904 --> 00:49:35,224
[clears throat]
Where are the gorillas?

699
00:49:36,304 --> 00:49:38,424
Go-ri-llas!

700
00:49:38,464 --> 00:49:40,424
Go-ri-llas!

701
00:49:40,464 --> 00:49:42,304
Shouting won't help,
Mr. Clayton.

702
00:49:42,384 --> 00:49:44,104
He doesn't
understand English.

703
00:49:44,144 --> 00:49:46,064
Then I'll make him understand.

704
00:49:46,104 --> 00:49:48,904
If I can teach a parrot
to sing God Save the Queen,

705
00:49:48,944 --> 00:49:52,904
I can certainly teach
this savage a thing or two.

706
00:49:53,904 --> 00:49:55,944
Gorilla.

707
00:49:57,184 --> 00:49:58,984
Gorilla.

708
00:49:59,064 --> 00:50:01,624
- [chuckles] He's got it!
- Gorilla.

709
00:50:01,704 --> 00:50:04,664
- Go-ril-la.
- Perhaps not.

710
00:50:04,744 --> 00:50:07,944
- Oh, no, no, no!
- Oh, no, no, no!

711
00:50:07,984 --> 00:50:10,544
Gimme that. Leave it.
STYLE
::cue()

712
00:50:10,624 --> 00:50:13,824
Mr. Clayton, I think
I'll take it from here.

713
00:50:23,384 --> 00:50:27,144
♪ Whatever you do
I'll do it too ♪

714
00:50:27,184 --> 00:50:31,344
♪ Show me everything
and tell me how ♪

715
00:50:31,424 --> 00:50:33,624
♪ It all means something ♪

716
00:50:33,704 --> 00:50:37,184
♪ And yet nothing to me ♪

717
00:50:39,624 --> 00:50:43,144
♪ I can see
there's so much to learn ♪

718
00:50:43,224 --> 00:50:47,464
♪ It's all so close
and yet so far ♪

719
00:50:47,504 --> 00:50:50,984
♪ I see myself
as people see me ♪

720
00:50:51,064 --> 00:50:55,464
♪ Oh, I just know there's
something bigger out there ♪

721
00:50:55,504 --> 00:50:59,464
♪ I wanna know
Can you show me ♪

722
00:50:59,504 --> 00:51:03,464
♪ I wanna know about
these strangers like me ♪

723
00:51:03,504 --> 00:51:07,424
♪ Tell me more
Please show me ♪

724
00:51:07,504 --> 00:51:11,504
♪ Something's familiar
about these strangers
like me ♪

725
00:51:19,704 --> 00:51:23,544
♪ Every gesture
Every move that she makes ♪

726
00:51:23,664 --> 00:51:27,544
♪ Makes me feel
like never before ♪

727
00:51:27,624 --> 00:51:33,424
♪ Why do I have this
growing need to be
beside her ♪

728
00:51:35,624 --> 00:51:38,944
♪ These emotions
I never knew ♪

729
00:51:39,024 --> 00:51:43,464
♪ Of some other world
far beyond this place ♪

730
00:51:43,544 --> 00:51:47,184
♪ Beyond the trees
Above the clouds ♪

731
00:51:47,224 --> 00:51:51,624
♪ I see before me
a new horizon ♪

732
00:51:51,704 --> 00:51:55,504
♪ I wanna know
Can you show me ♪

733
00:51:55,544 --> 00:51:59,704
♪ I wanna know about
these strangers like me ♪

734
00:51:59,704 --> 00:52:03,344
♪ Tell me more
Please show me ♪

735
00:52:03,384 --> 00:52:07,584
♪ Something's familiar
about these strangers
like me ♪

736
00:52:07,664 --> 00:52:12,704
♪ Come with me now
to see my world ♪

737
00:52:12,744 --> 00:52:16,744
♪ Where there's beauty
beyond your dreams ♪

738
00:52:16,824 --> 00:52:20,824
♪ Can you feel
the things I feel ♪

739
00:52:20,904 --> 00:52:25,064
♪ Right now, with you ♪

740
00:52:26,784 --> 00:52:29,064
♪ Take my hand ♪

741
00:52:29,104 --> 00:52:33,584
♪ There's a world
I need to know ♪

742
00:52:50,744 --> 00:52:53,384
[Clayton] We've wasted all
this time on what he wants.

743
00:52:53,464 --> 00:52:57,504
The boat could arrive any day.
Now, ask him straight out.

744
00:53:00,544 --> 00:53:04,424
Tarzan, will you take us
to the gorillas?

745
00:53:04,464 --> 00:53:06,584
[Jane] Do you understand?

746
00:53:06,624 --> 00:53:08,784
I understand.

747
00:53:08,824 --> 00:53:10,784
- Good work, Jane.
- Well?

748
00:53:10,864 --> 00:53:13,304
- I can't.
- What?

749
00:53:13,344 --> 00:53:16,584
- Why not, Tarzan?
- Kerchak.

750
00:53:19,704 --> 00:53:23,784
♪ I wanna know
Can you show me ♪

751
00:53:23,824 --> 00:53:27,664
♪ I wanna know about
these strangers like me ♪

752
00:53:27,744 --> 00:53:31,464
♪ Tell me more
Please show me ♪

753
00:53:31,584 --> 00:53:36,744
♪ Something's familiar
about these strangers
like me ♪
STYLE
::cue()

754
00:53:36,824 --> 00:53:38,904
♪ I wanna know ♪♪

755
00:53:56,104 --> 00:54:00,464
Oh, Terk,
I've never seen him so happy.

756
00:54:00,504 --> 00:54:02,544
Yeah? I give it a week.

757
00:54:06,184 --> 00:54:09,184
- [man 1] Aye, cut her loose!
- [man 2] Come on,
pull it down.

758
00:54:09,264 --> 00:54:11,464
[man 3] All right,
move it, ya bilge rats!

759
00:54:11,544 --> 00:54:12,944
[man 4] Heave ho, lads.

760
00:54:13,024 --> 00:54:15,264
[man 5] Put your back in it.
All right, move it.

761
00:54:15,344 --> 00:54:18,104
[Porter] Please, don't...
I've waited 30 years for this

762
00:54:18,184 --> 00:54:20,704
and I won't leave
until I see a gorilla.

763
00:54:20,744 --> 00:54:25,024
Isn't this dreadful, Tarzan?
No! No, no, wait!

764
00:54:25,064 --> 00:54:27,304
[man 6] Pick your barrel up.
Pick it up.

765
00:54:27,384 --> 00:54:29,384
[man 7] Here we go.
Here we go.

766
00:54:29,464 --> 00:54:32,984
[Clayton] You're the captain.
Tell them you've
had engine trouble,

767
00:54:33,064 --> 00:54:34,544
and give us two more days.

768
00:54:34,624 --> 00:54:37,064
And be late at every port
from here to London?

769
00:54:37,104 --> 00:54:38,664
We'll have come for nothing.

770
00:54:38,704 --> 00:54:42,464
I'm sorry, Miss Porter,
but I simply can't do it.

771
00:54:42,544 --> 00:54:45,104
[groans] This is your fault.

772
00:54:45,184 --> 00:54:46,904
I should've
followed my instincts

773
00:54:46,984 --> 00:54:48,664
and set traps for the beasts.

774
00:54:48,744 --> 00:54:51,544
Don't you think
I'm disappointed
about the gorillas?

775
00:54:51,544 --> 00:54:54,264
You are absolutely impossible!
[gasps]

776
00:54:54,344 --> 00:54:57,904
Tarzan. I was so afraid that
you wouldn't come in time.

777
00:54:57,944 --> 00:54:59,224
The boat's arrived.

778
00:54:59,304 --> 00:55:02,424
The boat that's come
to take us home, to England.

779
00:55:02,464 --> 00:55:06,904
And Daddy and I were...
Well, I was wondering...

780
00:55:06,984 --> 00:55:10,104
Well, we really hope
that you'll come with us.

781
00:55:10,104 --> 00:55:11,584
Won't you?

782
00:55:12,784 --> 00:55:15,904
Go see England today.
Come home tomorrow.

783
00:55:15,944 --> 00:55:17,944
Oh, no.

784
00:55:18,024 --> 00:55:21,264
Well, see, it would be very
difficult to come back...

785
00:55:21,344 --> 00:55:22,584
...ever.

786
00:55:22,624 --> 00:55:24,224
Not come back?

787
00:55:24,264 --> 00:55:28,264
I know it sounds awful,
but you belong with us,
with people.

788
00:55:28,344 --> 00:55:30,304
Jane must stay with Tarzan.

789
00:55:30,384 --> 00:55:33,744
Stay here? Oh, no, no, no...
My laundry.

790
00:55:33,784 --> 00:55:37,264
No, I can't stay.
Look, I've got...

791
00:55:37,304 --> 00:55:39,744
I'm with my father, and...

792
00:55:39,784 --> 00:55:43,544
Jane... stay.

793
00:55:43,624 --> 00:55:45,904
- But...
- Please.

794
00:55:48,344 --> 00:55:50,824
But, I can't.

795
00:55:50,904 --> 00:55:53,184
[sobbing]

796
00:55:53,264 --> 00:55:55,264
[Clayton] Women.
[chuckles]

797
00:55:55,304 --> 00:55:58,144
How typical.
Thank you, Jones.

798
00:55:58,184 --> 00:56:02,224
Even if you hadn't grown up
a savage, you'd be lost.

799
00:56:02,304 --> 00:56:05,784
There are no trails
through a woman's heart.

800
00:56:05,864 --> 00:56:09,424
- Jane is going.
- Yes.

801
00:56:09,464 --> 00:56:13,624
If only she could've spent
more time with the gorillas.

802
00:56:13,664 --> 00:56:15,984
She's so disappointed.

803
00:56:16,024 --> 00:56:18,824
Crushed, really.

804
00:56:18,904 --> 00:56:21,904
Sorry, old boy.

805
00:56:21,984 --> 00:56:25,384
Oh, well, I'd best get
Jane's things to the ship.

806
00:56:29,584 --> 00:56:30,664
Clayton.

807
00:56:33,144 --> 00:56:36,424
If Jane sees gorillas,
she stays?

808
00:56:36,504 --> 00:56:40,224
Say, that's why she came,
isn't it?

809
00:56:42,384 --> 00:56:45,024
- I'll do it.
- Good man!

810
00:56:45,064 --> 00:56:46,584
- Snipes?
- Sir?

811
00:56:46,664 --> 00:56:51,344
Get the boys together. There's
gonna be a change in plans.
STYLE
::cue()

812
00:56:51,424 --> 00:56:53,424
Terk, just get
Kerchak out of the way.

813
00:56:53,504 --> 00:56:55,464
- What?
- I'd be happy to get...

814
00:56:55,504 --> 00:56:59,144
Hey! Shut your trunk
and get me out of here.

815
00:56:59,184 --> 00:57:01,544
[Terk]
Can you believe that guy?

816
00:57:01,584 --> 00:57:05,024
Drops us like a newborn
giraffe, kerplop!

817
00:57:05,064 --> 00:57:08,544
Now waltzes in here
and expects us to just...

818
00:57:08,624 --> 00:57:11,224
Terk, I'm asking you
as a friend.

819
00:57:11,344 --> 00:57:13,864
[groans]

820
00:57:13,944 --> 00:57:16,744
With the face and the eyes
and the...

821
00:57:16,824 --> 00:57:21,384
All right! But don't make me
do anything embarrassing.

822
00:57:22,184 --> 00:57:24,104
I'm gonna kill him!!

823
00:57:24,184 --> 00:57:27,504
I thought that dress
was rather slimming on you.

824
00:57:27,544 --> 00:57:30,424
Really? I thought it was
a little revealing
and kind of...

825
00:57:30,504 --> 00:57:32,384
- [loud roar]
- [screaming]

826
00:57:33,704 --> 00:57:35,904
How does she move
in this thing?

827
00:57:39,304 --> 00:57:41,304
[Terk] Look out!

828
00:58:06,744 --> 00:58:09,864
- Look, Daddy!
- [stammering] Where?

829
00:58:09,944 --> 00:58:12,944
Jane. [panting]

830
00:58:13,024 --> 00:58:15,384
[Clayton] Now, be careful,
professor.

831
00:58:15,424 --> 00:58:17,224
[Porter] Mustn't,
mustn't frighten.

832
00:58:17,264 --> 00:58:20,504
She's beautiful.

833
00:58:20,624 --> 00:58:22,744
She's my mother.

834
00:58:22,784 --> 00:58:26,144
But... This is your...

835
00:58:27,464 --> 00:58:29,144
...mother?

836
00:58:33,224 --> 00:58:35,344
[soft hooting]

837
00:58:38,784 --> 00:58:41,944
- [stammering]
What's happening?
- I don't know, Daddy.

838
00:58:42,024 --> 00:58:44,144
Oh! It's getting away!

839
00:58:44,184 --> 00:58:46,744
No! You'll only
frighten her more.

840
00:58:50,904 --> 00:58:52,904
[hooting]

841
00:58:54,304 --> 00:58:58,144
Yes, absolutely, my dear.
Good idea.

842
00:58:58,224 --> 00:59:00,384
What are you doing?
Want to frighten them?

843
00:59:00,464 --> 00:59:02,624
Get up. Get...

844
00:59:02,664 --> 00:59:04,944
Don't get up.

845
00:59:26,144 --> 00:59:29,184
[stammering] Oh!

846
00:59:32,104 --> 00:59:33,864
[grunting]

847
00:59:36,104 --> 00:59:37,344
Hello.

848
00:59:42,344 --> 00:59:44,864
It's very nice
to meet you, too.

849
00:59:48,824 --> 00:59:52,224
Oh, Your Majesty,
you're such a tease.

850
00:59:52,344 --> 00:59:55,104
Whoa! Hello. Hello.

851
00:59:55,184 --> 00:59:58,264
Archimedes Q. Porter
at your service.

852
00:59:58,344 --> 01:00:00,864
Quite a grip you've got.

853
01:00:00,944 --> 01:00:04,184
Oh, thank you, yes.
Is that one of mine?

854
01:00:05,784 --> 01:00:07,664
This is wonderful,
Mr. Clayton!

855
01:00:07,704 --> 01:00:09,384
Look, look! Social grooming.

856
01:00:09,464 --> 01:00:12,664
Congratulations, professor.

857
01:00:12,704 --> 01:00:15,984
Our dream has come true.
STYLE
::cue()

858
01:00:19,824 --> 01:00:21,224
Give me that!

859
01:00:21,264 --> 01:00:23,744
Hey, what are you doing?
Now, stop that! Stop!

860
01:00:23,784 --> 01:00:25,384
Hold on now. Leave that!

861
01:00:25,464 --> 01:00:27,664
That is not to be played with!

862
01:00:42,464 --> 01:00:43,904
Can you teach me?

863
01:00:43,944 --> 01:00:47,264
- Speak gorilla?
- Hmm. Yes.

864
01:00:49,104 --> 01:00:51,984
[Tarzan grunts,
Jane repeats]

865
01:01:08,744 --> 01:01:12,184
Good heavens, what did I say?

866
01:01:12,264 --> 01:01:15,464
That Jane stays with Tarzan.

867
01:01:15,504 --> 01:01:18,944
Stay? But I...
I thought we'd already...

868
01:01:18,984 --> 01:01:21,664
- Tarzan, I...
- [Terk] Whoa!

869
01:01:26,344 --> 01:01:29,344
- Is that my dress?
- Oh, no.

870
01:01:29,424 --> 01:01:31,104
[roaring]

871
01:01:33,344 --> 01:01:34,384
[Jane] Daddy.

872
01:01:37,944 --> 01:01:39,784
Give it to me!

873
01:01:42,944 --> 01:01:43,944
Go!

874
01:02:02,424 --> 01:02:03,504
Go!

875
01:02:05,224 --> 01:02:07,064
Wait, wait! Tarzan!

876
01:02:07,184 --> 01:02:08,344
Go now!

877
01:02:08,384 --> 01:02:11,664
Jane, quickly! Hurry!
Come along!

878
01:02:18,064 --> 01:02:20,304
[both panting]

879
01:02:30,864 --> 01:02:34,864
Kerchak, I didn't...
I'm sorry, I...

880
01:02:34,944 --> 01:02:38,544
I asked you
to protect our family.

881
01:02:38,584 --> 01:02:41,704
And you betrayed us all.

882
01:03:10,064 --> 01:03:12,224
I'm so confused.

883
01:03:14,784 --> 01:03:16,424
Come with me.

884
01:03:16,424 --> 01:03:19,784
There's something I should've
shown you long ago.
STYLE
::cue()

885
01:04:15,424 --> 01:04:16,984
[glass breaking]

886
01:04:39,664 --> 01:04:41,504
Is this me?

887
01:04:45,704 --> 01:04:47,784
And this is my father,

888
01:04:47,824 --> 01:04:49,384
and...

889
01:04:49,464 --> 01:04:51,264
and my...

890
01:04:52,824 --> 01:04:54,824
Now you know.

891
01:04:54,864 --> 01:04:59,264
Tarzan, I just want you
to be happy,

892
01:04:59,344 --> 01:05:02,064
whatever you decide.

893
01:05:49,544 --> 01:05:53,744
No matter where I go,
you will always be my mother.

894
01:05:53,824 --> 01:05:56,064
[sobbing]

895
01:05:58,224 --> 01:06:01,744
And you will always be
in my heart.

896
01:06:21,344 --> 01:06:23,824
Goodbye, Tarzan.

897
01:06:23,944 --> 01:06:26,104
- [Jane] Tarzan!
- [men shouting]

898
01:06:26,184 --> 01:06:28,224
I'm so glad you
found us in time.

899
01:06:37,624 --> 01:06:39,424
Tarzan!

900
01:06:39,464 --> 01:06:42,504
We're too late!
I can't believe it!

901
01:06:42,584 --> 01:06:44,704
If you had pulled over
and asked for directions...

902
01:06:44,784 --> 01:06:46,824
We didn't get to say goodbye.

903
01:06:46,904 --> 01:06:50,264
Well, good riddance,
all right?
Who needs you, huh?

904
01:06:50,384 --> 01:06:52,424
Go on, get out of here,
bald boy!

905
01:06:52,464 --> 01:06:55,344
You, you ingrate!
You bald ingrate!

906
01:06:55,424 --> 01:06:57,424
Go on and rot, for all I care!

907
01:06:57,464 --> 01:06:59,184
Go!

908
01:07:01,304 --> 01:07:03,264
What are you looking at?

909
01:07:03,304 --> 01:07:05,224
I'm gonna miss him, too.

910
01:07:13,464 --> 01:07:16,584
[Jane] Tarzan,
you can't imagine
what's in store for you.
STYLE
::cue()
[Jane] Tarzan,
you can't imagine
what's in store for you.

911
01:07:16,664 --> 01:07:17,944
You'll see the world.

912
01:07:17,984 --> 01:07:19,744
Everyone's going
to want to meet you.

913
01:07:19,824 --> 01:07:21,984
Kings, scientists,
famous writers.

914
01:07:22,064 --> 01:07:25,344
Yes. Darwin and Kipling.
Queen Victoria!

915
01:07:25,464 --> 01:07:27,744
I haven't met her,
but I heard she's nice.

916
01:07:27,824 --> 01:07:29,464
And I'll be with Jane?

917
01:07:31,664 --> 01:07:34,384
Yes, with Jane.
[chuckles]

918
01:07:35,344 --> 01:07:37,624
Oh! Slippery.

919
01:07:57,064 --> 01:07:59,824
- [sinister laughing]
- [Jane] Tarzan!

920
01:07:59,864 --> 01:08:02,144
- Ow!
- Tarzan!

921
01:08:02,184 --> 01:08:03,624
[man] Get him!

922
01:08:09,744 --> 01:08:11,824
- [Jane] Tarzan!
- [Tarzan] Jane!

923
01:08:29,184 --> 01:08:32,224
- [struggling]
- [gunshot]

924
01:08:32,264 --> 01:08:34,064
What's going on here?

925
01:08:34,104 --> 01:08:36,424
Clayton! Clayton, help!

926
01:08:38,224 --> 01:08:40,104
Have we met?

927
01:08:43,464 --> 01:08:47,264
Ah, yes, the ape man.

928
01:08:47,944 --> 01:08:50,424
Clayton, you...

929
01:08:50,544 --> 01:08:51,584
You...

930
01:08:53,224 --> 01:08:55,784
So sorry about the rude
welcome, old boy,

931
01:08:55,864 --> 01:08:57,904
but I couldn't have you
making a scene

932
01:08:57,944 --> 01:09:02,064
when we put your furry friends
in their cages.

933
01:09:02,184 --> 01:09:03,664
Why?

934
01:09:04,264 --> 01:09:05,424
Why?

935
01:09:05,464 --> 01:09:08,264
For three hundred pounds
sterling a head.

936
01:09:08,304 --> 01:09:11,744
Actually, I have you
to thank, my boy.

937
01:09:11,824 --> 01:09:14,904
Couldn't have done it
without you.

938
01:09:17,064 --> 01:09:19,264
Lock him up with the others.

939
01:09:20,464 --> 01:09:22,304
No!

940
01:09:23,984 --> 01:09:25,664
That sounded like Tarzan.

941
01:09:25,744 --> 01:09:28,064
He sounded like
he was in trouble.

942
01:09:28,104 --> 01:09:30,144
Yeah, well, why doesn't
he get his new friends

943
01:09:30,224 --> 01:09:31,704
to help him?
I don't care.

944
01:09:32,904 --> 01:09:35,104
That's it!

945
01:09:35,184 --> 01:09:38,264
I've had it with you
and your emotional
constipation!

946
01:09:38,384 --> 01:09:41,304
Tarzan needs us
and we're gonna help him!

947
01:09:41,344 --> 01:09:45,424
You got that? Now, pipe down
and hang on tight!

948
01:09:45,464 --> 01:09:47,624
We've got a boat to catch.

949
01:09:47,704 --> 01:09:50,024
[bugle call]

950
01:09:56,344 --> 01:09:59,944
[sputtering, coughing]
I've never felt so alive!

951
01:09:59,984 --> 01:10:02,744
Good! 'Cause I'm
gonna kill you!

952
01:10:02,824 --> 01:10:04,984
No time for that now, missy.

953
01:10:15,144 --> 01:10:17,384
[radar pings]

954
01:10:19,224 --> 01:10:20,944
[shouting]

955
01:10:25,344 --> 01:10:27,464
Tarzan, it's no use. Don't!

956
01:10:36,024 --> 01:10:38,984
- Clayton.
- Yes, Clayton.

957
01:10:39,024 --> 01:10:43,184
Clayton betrayed us all.
I'm so sorry, Tarzan.

958
01:10:43,264 --> 01:10:45,944
No, I did this.

959
01:10:46,024 --> 01:10:50,504
I betrayed my family.
Kerchak was right.

960
01:10:50,584 --> 01:10:55,384
Those magnificent creatures,
shivering in cages.

961
01:10:55,504 --> 01:10:58,344
What is this world coming to?

962
01:11:03,864 --> 01:11:06,544
Oh, by Jove!
Don't know my own strength.

963
01:11:08,864 --> 01:11:10,704
[shouting]
STYLE
::cue()

964
01:11:11,544 --> 01:11:13,064
What was that?

965
01:11:13,144 --> 01:11:16,024
- [Terk] You are an animal!
- [trumpets]

966
01:11:17,584 --> 01:11:19,544
That sounded
just like an elephant.

967
01:11:19,584 --> 01:11:20,824
Tantor!

968
01:11:22,544 --> 01:11:23,624
Thanks, guys.

969
01:11:23,704 --> 01:11:26,584
I thought I would never
see you again!

970
01:11:26,664 --> 01:11:29,024
And here you are.

971
01:11:29,064 --> 01:11:32,344
Sometimes you embarrass me.

972
01:11:43,024 --> 01:11:45,904
[sniffs, grunts]

973
01:11:58,904 --> 01:12:01,264
[men shouting]

974
01:12:39,744 --> 01:12:42,904
Ah! I remember you.

975
01:12:44,504 --> 01:12:47,144
I think this one
will be better off stuffed.

976
01:12:49,264 --> 01:12:51,904
[Tarzan yelling]

977
01:13:09,144 --> 01:13:10,864
You came back.

978
01:13:10,944 --> 01:13:12,504
I came home.

979
01:13:24,384 --> 01:13:25,664
[evil laugh]

980
01:13:27,504 --> 01:13:29,304
Fire!

981
01:13:35,384 --> 01:13:37,824
You there! Take what you can
back to the boat.

982
01:13:37,864 --> 01:13:39,184
Aye, aye, sir.

983
01:13:41,624 --> 01:13:44,064
I've got some hunting to do.

984
01:14:04,904 --> 01:14:07,384
[frantic hooting]

985
01:14:08,384 --> 01:14:09,584
Don't worry.

986
01:14:09,664 --> 01:14:12,104
I'm going to have you
out of this in a second.

987
